    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0629" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg415"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 195.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Moran to Mr. Fish</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 123.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 8, 1870</date>. (Received December
                    22.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In connection with Mr. Motley’s dispatches
                    Nos. 517 and 519, I have now the honor to inclose herewith copies extracted from
                    The Daily News and Times, in English and French, of Prince Gortchakoff’s reply,
                    dated the 20th of November, to Earl Granville’s note of the 31st October, on the
                    subject of the revision of the treaty of Paris of 1856, together with copy of
                    Earl Granville’s answer, dated the 28th November.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BENJAMIN MORAN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d213-a1.xml" xpointer="d213-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d213-a2.xml" xpointer="d213-a2"/>
